Checkout now clears the cart when an `OrderCreated` message arrives, and retries a failed delete before it gives up.

An `OrderCreated` message on `order.created.queue` looks up the checkout in `checkout_db.checkouts` by `payment_reference`. A new message sets the status to `order_created` and stores `order_id`, then calls `DELETE /cart/{cart_id}`. Success (204 or 404) sets the status to `cart_cleared`. A 500, 503, or network error waits 5s, 10s, and 20s, up to 3 retries. If those attempts all fail, the status stays `order_created` and the failure is logged. A repeat message for `order_created` or `cart_cleared` is acknowledged and does not delete the cart again. The consumer only reads and writes `checkout_db`.

The app starts that consumer on startup. The existing RabbitMQ helper and `checkouts` collection were already in place, so those files were left as they are.

